WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.200
Why does this matter?

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.017
The example guide's fourth gap:

3
00:00:03.017 --> 00:00:06.798
SailPoint reads the HR system
and can provision the directory,

4
00:00:06.798 --> 00:00:11.450
while the workbook's design makes Entra
inbound provisioning the one writer.

5
00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:14.687
The guide's advice is to pick
one writer per attribute.

6
00:00:14.687 --> 00:00:19.840
Either Entra inbound provisioning stays the
door and SailPoint governs entitlements,

7
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.663
or SailPoint becomes the
provisioning service.

8
00:00:22.663 --> 00:00:23.638
Not both.

9
00:00:23.638 --> 00:00:26.921
Until now, the drift client
saw only the symptom,

10
00:00:26.921 --> 00:00:30.037
drift that keeps coming
back, never the cause.

11
00:00:30.037 --> 00:00:35.540
Both configurations export as JSON,
so the check can run on files, today.
